			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T00:18:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1041,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Add SkyEvent registry and extend Channel registry with legacy channels\n\nAdd Source/IPC/SkyEvent.ts as a TypeScript mirror of the Rust SkyEvent enum in Element/Common/Source/IPC/SkyEvent.rs. This registry provides type-safe constants for all 95 Tauri event URIs that Mountain emits (e.g., \"sky://extensions/installed\"), replacing free-text strings in Wind service subscriptions.\n\nExtend Channel.ts with three legacy channels that don't follow the `prefix:method` convention:\n- `MountainGetStatus` (\"mountain_get_status\") — snake_case Tauri command\n- `UserInterfaceShowOpenDialog` (\"UserInterface.ShowOpenDialog\") — dotted gRPC name\n- `UserInterfaceShowSaveDialog` (\"UserInterface.ShowSaveDialog\") — dotted gRPC name\n\nRelax the Channel registry type from `${string}:${string}` to `string` to accommodate these historical shapes. Update all call sites:\n- MountainImplementation.ts: `mountain_get_status` → `Channel.MountainGetStatus`\n- Files/Live.ts: ShowOpenDialog/ShowSaveDialog → Channel registry\n- Workspaces/Live.ts: \"sky://workspaces/changed\" → `SkyEvent.WorkspacesChanged`\n\nAlso add ExtensionChangeStream.ts which merges the install/uninstall event streams into a single typed Effect-TS Stream, enabling the sidebar to subscribe to extension lifecycle changes via the SkyEvent registry.\n\nCompile-time validation now catches drift between Mountain's emit URIs and Wind's subscribe calls.",
			"SHA": "a12e2caea303a8db52560d9eb51f06f768ab74be"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T00:08:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1039,
				21
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Use Channel registry for all IPC invokes across Wind services\n\nRefactor all 19 Wind service Live layers to use the IPC Channel registry instead of free-text string literals, ensuring compile-time validation against typos at every call site.\n\nThis completes the migration started in the previous commit (which added InstallVsix/Uninstall to ExtensionsService using the Channel registry). Now every service layer in Wind uses typed Channel imports:\n- Commands, Decorations, Files, History, Keybinding, Label, Lifecycle, Model\n- Notification, Output, Progress, QuickInput, Search, Storage, Terminal\n- TextFile, Themes, WorkingCopy, Workspaces\n\nAlso extend Source/IPC/Channel.ts with newly-defined channels for TextFile (read/write/save), WorkingCopy (dirty-state tracking), and QuickInput (showInputBox/showQuickPick) to complete the registry coverage.\n\nOne exception remains: `mountain_get_status` in MountainImplementation.ts uses a snake_case wire string that doesn't fit the `prefix:method` convention, documented as TODO for a future coordinated rename.",
			"SHA": "8244ad244acdea3e3eccfae5c308b697ea2afbfe"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-21T23:37:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1039,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add InstallVsix and Uninstall to ExtensionsService\n\nImplement the Atom K5 contract by adding InstallVsix and Uninstall methods\nto the ExtensionsService interface and Live layer. InstallVsix accepts a\n.vsix path (plain or file:// URI) and returns the ILocalExtension envelope\nfrom Mountain. Uninstall accepts an extension identifier and resolves with\ntrue after Mountain removes the install directory and broadcasts the\nuninstalled event.\n\nAlso refactor all IPC invokes to use the Channel registry\n(Element/Wind/Source/IPC/Channel.ts) instead of free-text string literals,\nensuring compile-time validation against typos. Affected operations:\nGetExtension, GetAllExtensions, IsActive, Activate.\n\nThe prior implementation was a no-op stub that silently returned null,\nleaving the \"Install from VSIX…\" prompt and sidebar Uninstall button\nnon-functional. These now resolve through real handlers in\nWindServiceHandler/Extension.rs.",
			"SHA": "86bd4240706a77d5d2cea5337b4006bb9dccf625"
		}
	],
